down_beta desc: Systematic tail-sensitivity: for each asset, regress daily returns on SPX returns restricted to sessions where SPX closed lower (market-down days only), using a 60-observation rolling window over the down-day series. Higher values mark assets that fall hardest when the market falls; positive IC means higher downside beta assets tended to earn higher forward 10d returns in this window.

dd_duration desc: Log1p of number of days since the last 120-day rolling high, then cross-sectionally orthogonalized (per-date) against z-scored mom_120d_skip5. Captures mean-reversion/recovery pressure after prolonged drawdowns independent of raw momentum.
